		<item>
			<title>Version 1.3.7</title>
			<sparkle:version>24</sparkle:version>
			<sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
			<link>https://github.com/arunyagoojar/Mac-XCloud/releases/tag/v1.3.7-b24</link>
			<sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>12.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
			<description><![CDATA[<h2>Mac Xcloud 1.3.7</h2>
<h3>Steering and controller feedback</h3>
<ul>
<li>Improved steering-wheel motion tracking: gyro prediction follows quick turns while absolute sensor correction reduces accelerometer jolts and keeps held turns steady.</li>
<li>Preserved gyro aiming, touchpad aiming and bidirectional flick shifting. For flick shifting, enable manual gears and map right-stick up to upshift and right-stick down to downshift inside the game.</li>
<li>Replaced the default adaptive-trigger menu with twelve designs: Acceleration Pedal, Brake Pedal, Pistol, Revolver, Rifle, Automatic Weapon, Bow, Crossbow, Shield, Chainsaw, Flashlight and Engine Start.</li>
<li>Added pressure-driven haptic rhythms, pistol/bow release feedback and bounded recoil resistance. Existing saved and custom effects remain loadable.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Settings and navigation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Removed the persistent on-screen Back and Home buttons.</li>
<li>Added Backspace for browsing back, with protection for typing, text editing and gameplay. Existing Mac navigation shortcuts remain available.</li>
<li>Listed app shortcuts in Settings → App → About.</li>
<li>The menu bar status icon is removed as soon as the app quits.</li>
<li>Fixed immediate OLED background updates and made global settings show when a reload is needed.</li>
<li>Removed remaining keyboard/mouse gaming settings. WKWebView limitations made reliable gaming support impractical; ordinary typing, clicking and app shortcuts remain available.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Profiles and usability</h3>
<ul>
<li>Per-game profile recall restores controller, motion, trigger and selected picture/audio settings, using game IDs with website-title fallback.</li>
<li>Native settings use five main groups, with advanced steering controls and diagnostics collapsed.</li>
<li>Rewrote the README with the current feature list, controller requirements, limitations and a Forza Horizon 5 cruising setup.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Compatibility and remote play</h3>
<ul>
<li>Verified Intel and Apple Silicon compilation and added a release check requiring both executable architectures.</li>
<li>Fixed console-list readiness and refreshes stale console status when reopening Remote Play.</li>
<li>Xbox waking from standby remains unresolved; streaming from an already powered-on console is supported.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Notes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Trigger effects are local simulations, not weapon telemetry from Xbox games. Hardware resistance zones and scheduled haptics approximate the requested effects.</li>
<li>Steering feel depends on your controller, connection, car and in-game settings. The user has confirmed the revised steering is usable; further tuning is personal.</li>
<li>Automatic-update dialogs now display these release notes instead of a commit hash.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
			<pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 21:59:47 +0000</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://github.com/arunyagoojar/Mac-XCloud/releases/download/v1.3.7-b24/MacXcloud.zip" sparkle:edSignature="1oNPm/SjTn+T6jFDX27Ugb97vfOw90VdB+WRkDDI0i1nqjSUp/Zx/2UytHlj+mbF12ZPeSo/icaJ8JmddJ5LDw==" length="5387092" type="application/octet-stream" />
